<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Ishkuza</h1><p class="st-meta">680 BCE – 615 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Scythian kingdom in north-western Iran that troubled and then allied with Assyria, remembered by Herodotus for a 28-year Scythian domination of Asia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Scythian horsemen from the steppes north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> entered the lands south of the Caucasus and around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-urmia">Lake Urmia</a> in the early 7th century BCE. Assyrian texts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/esarhaddon">Esarhaddon</a> call their kingdom Ishkuza and name its leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishpakai">Ishpakai</a>, who was killed fighting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> around 675 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Ishkuza were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mounted-archer">mounted archers</a> who raided widely and sold their services to neighbouring powers. Their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartatua">Bartatua</a>, identified with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>' Protothyes, sought an Assyrian princess in marriage, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> thereafter generally supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cimmerians">Cimmerians</a>. Herodotus says that under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madyes">Madyes</a>, son of Protothyes, the Scythians defeated the Medes and dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-roman-province">Asia</a> for 28 years. Their own institutions are known only through outsiders' reports.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, the Median king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyaxares">Cyaxares</a> killed the Scythian leaders at a banquet and drove them out, after which the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/median-empire">Median Empire</a> absorbed their lands. The chronology of these events is uncertain.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 680 BCE – 615 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesopotamia and Iran</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:46.17%;width:1.29%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>680 BCE – 615 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ishpakai, Bartatua, Madyes</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Scythian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Scythian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Iran, Azerbaijan</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Scythian kingdom of Ishkuza, Ashguzai, Iskuza</dd></dl></aside></div>

